DuoMatching
Joint–Marginal Distribution Matching for Few-Step Video Generation
https://johnzhan2023.github.io/DuoMatching/

The video runtime and training implementation derive from Causal Forcing
(https://github.com/thu-ml/Causal-Forcing), including its Self Forcing foundations.
This release was prepared from the local Causal-Forcing adapter branch,
commit ebede21, with portable paths, packaging, strict checkpoint loading,
and LatentBridge integration added for the DuoMatching release.

LatentBridge source is included as latent_bridge/ with its preprocessing and
training entry points under scripts/latent_bridge/.

wan/ retains the Wan Team copyright notices. Wan's CLIP implementation identifies
its OpenAI CLIP and OpenCLIP origins in the source. Existing attribution is
retained. demo_utils/memory.py derives from lllyasviel/FramePack under Apache-2.0. The repository's Apache-2.0 LICENSE is carried forward.

Upstream weights are downloaded separately, and their licenses remain applicable.
No datasets, private services, experiment logs or third-party model weights are
bundled in the code repository.
